# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit any of these
#
# Git history is permanent. Deleting a secret in a later commit does NOT
# remove it: it stays in the history, and GitHub caches and indexes contents.
# The only safe move is never committing it in the first place. Anything that
# does slip through must be treated as compromised and rotated, not deleted.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# App signing. Losing the keystore means this app can never be updated on Play
# again; leaking it means someone else can sign releases as you. Keep backups
# somewhere private and off this machine.
android/key.properties
key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx

